, but trailed her three teammates and was not advanced. Defending champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/11488"} "Nicole Uphoff"] " had also won the 1990 World Championship and in Barcelona, became the second dressage rider to defend her gold medal, after Sweden’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/12678"} "Henri Saint Cyr"] " in 1952-56, but Saint Cyr won his gold medals on two different horses, as " [:a {:href "/horses/2076"} "Rembrandt"] ", under Uphoff, became the first horse to defend a gold medal in this event. " [:a {:href "/athletes/11503"} "Isabell Werth"] " won the silver medal but would improve and win gold at Atlanta in 1996. " [:a {:href "/athletes/11583"} "Klaus Balkenhol"] " won bronze while the top non-German was fourth-placed Dutchwoman " [:a {:href "/athletes/11490"} "Anky van Grunsven"] ", who would win a silver medal in this event in 1996, and then gold medals in 2000, 2004, and 2008."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "Horse"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Grand Prix"] [:th {} "Grand Prix Special"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "432"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/11488"} "Nicole Uphoff-Becker"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/2076"} "Rembrandt"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "1,626"] [:td {} "1,768 (1)"] [:td {} "1,626 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "428"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/11503"} "Isabell Werth"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/1002"} "Gigolo"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] 